kind of problem, so it fails in every non-dev environment. Quick fix. Bundle it with 00016. |\n\n## ⚠️ Warn (18)\n\n**High severity but low agent_risk.** These are real problems, but they're about maintainability or assets, not correctness:\n- **00033** `generateInvoice` is 204 lines: severity 0.90, agent_risk 0.13. Not blocking, but it's new code, so ask for it to be split.\n- **00035** SVG with embedded rasters: severity 0.75, agent_risk 0.08. Only affects the asset.\n\n**Medium severity, agent_risk ≥ 0.15:**\n\n| ID | Finding | sev | agent_risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 00001 | 6 direct clock reads in `date.ts`, 1 of which decides a branch | 0.60 | 0.45 |\n| 00003 | No AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md / SKILL.md, though a `messy` bin is declared | 0.60 | 0.43 |\n| 00004 | `\"enterprise\"` literal repeated across 4 areas | 0.50 | 0.43 |\n| 00006 | `/settings/billing` has two nav labels (Plans / Billing) | 0.60 | 0.39 |\n| 00007 | Route metadata drift on `/settings/billing` (4 different names) | 0.60 | 0.39 |\n| 00009 | Date strings parsed without a timezone (L29, L33) | 0.60 | 0.38 |\n| 00012 | `calculateRefundPreview` sends email and writes an audit record | 0.55 | 0.35 |\n| 00013 | Refund authorisation rule exists only in a comment | 0.50 | 0.35 |\n| 00014 | Day math uses a fixed 86400000 ms, which breaks across DST changes | 0.60 | 0.33 |\n| 00017 | One concept called tenant/account/team/workspace/organisation | 0.55 | 0.31 |\n| 00025 | Test with no assertions | 0.45 | 0.28 |\n| 00028 | Commented-out refund code | 0.45 | 0.24 |\n| 00029 | 7 clock reads in `billing.ts` (recording only) | 0.60 | 0.24 |\n\nThree of these are more urgent than the table suggests:\n- **00012 and 00013** together mean a function named \"preview\" has side effects, and the rule about who may approve a refund isn't enforced in code.\n- **00009** sits in the same file as blocker 00005. Fix them in the same pass.\n\n**Low severity but high agent_risk (≥ 0.35):**\n- **00002** `resolvePaymentResult` ret